**Assumption 1.2 (explicit structural primitive).** Use SSA Assumption 3.1's
seven reciprocal endpoint slots
$\mathsf P,\mathsf L,\mathsf R,\mathsf O_0,\mathsf O_1,
\mathsf H_0,\mathsf H_1$ and its bounded atomic patch convention.
A patch follows specified bounded root walks, inspects finite components,
uses a finite truth table, assigns a bounded endpoint list, constructs a
bounded template, and commits one native core/control/receipt occurrence.
Charge every probe, every designated assignment including unchanged values
and empty-slot initialization, every created vertex, and the commitment.
Internal endpoint assignments are not additional observable cuts.

The distinguished root, finite routing foundation and finite rule mechanism
are charged primitive apparatus. They contain no initial source value or
future capacity advice. They do not constitute an implementation of atomic
patches by ordinary RD/WR, and provide no new actor read or history entry.
The native guard, owner, input/output restriction and prescribed row remain
necessary. The model's one-head ordinary-tape and two-head meter cursor
relations, including partial boot construction, remain its actual primitive
cursor relations. No additional raw-code opcode for creating arbitrary
heads, runtime pointers or whole-word effects is admitted.

As in ARC Assumption 1.2, completion assertions require actual finite input
at its prescribed sites and termination of each reached original local
controller/prior computation. A finite-prefix assertion requires only the
actual prefix. No uniform deadline or infinite supply is assumed.

